  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Myanmar Earthquake Appeal Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Myanmar Earthquake Appeal Phase II will build on the Phase I intervention ,  feedback and lessons learned from CAREs staff, partners Treasure Land Development Association (TLDA) and Disability Inclusion Oriented - Yatwonthit (DIOY) - Organisation for People with Disability (OPD), alongside post distribution monitoring (PDM) from community members. Phase II will prioritise recovery and resilience, directly supporting 500 households (1,460 individuals) through:
&#x2022;	Shelter support (cash or voucher): Repair and rebuilding assistance for 100 households (420 individuals).
&#x2022;	Livelihood restoration: Inputs (cash or vouchers) for 200 households (840 individuals) to restart small businesses and agricultural activities.
&#x2022;	Mainstreamed protection: Gender-based violence (GBV) awareness and safety support for 500 individuals from 500 households.
&#x2022;	Mainstreamed Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR): DRR awareness activities for 100 individuals from 100 households</narrative>
  </description>
